# 2. Update Master Layout to include licensing footer\
cat << 'EOF' > _layouts/default.html\
<!DOCTYPE html>\
<html lang="en">\
<head>\
    <meta charset="UTF-8">\
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">\
    <title>{{ page.title }}</title>\
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/styles.css' | relative_url }}">\
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="{{ '/favicon.svg' | relative_url }}">\
    <script src="https://unpkg.com/lucide@latest"></script>\
    <script>\
        const theme = localStorage.getItem('theme') || (window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light');\
        document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', theme);\
    </script>\
</head>\
<body>\
    <main>\
        <div class="header-nav">\
            <button onclick="toggleTheme()" class="theme-toggle" aria-label="Toggle Theme">\
                <i data-lucide="sun" class="sun-icon"></i>\
                <i data-lucide="moon" class="moon-icon"></i>\
            </button>\
        </div>\
        \
        {{ content }}\
        \
        <footer style="margin-top: 4rem; padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--surface0); font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--subtext0); text-align: center; line-height: 1.5;">\
            <p>Site infrastructure and code are licensed under <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GPLv3</a>.</p>\
            <p>All written content and logs are licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-NC-ND 4.0</a>.</p>\
        </footer>\
    </main>\
\
    <script>\
        lucide.createIcons();\
        function toggleTheme() {\
            const current = document.documentElement.getAttribute('data-theme');\
            const next = current === 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark';\
            document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', next);\
            localStorage.setItem('theme', next);\
        }\
    </script>\
</body>\
</html>\
EOF\
\
# 3. Create the README.md Documentation\
cat << 'EOF' > README.md\
# Digital Garden & Logbook\
\
A minimalist, text-focused digital garden built with Jekyll and typeset for readability on the small web. \
\
## Licensing\
* **Code & Infrastructure:** [GPLv3](LICENSE)\
* **Written Content:** [CC BY-NC-ND 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/)\
\
## Project Structure\
```text\
rudraasthana.github.io/\
âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ _layouts/\
âƒ´‚   âƒ´ƒ´âƒ´€âƒ´€ default.html         # Master template with theme toggle & footer\
âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ _posts/\
âƒ´‚   âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ blog/\
âƒ´‚   âƒ´‚   âƒ´ƒ´âƒ´€âƒ´€ YYYY-MM-DD-title.md  ( * as many logs as published * )\
âƒ´‚   âƒ´ƒ´âƒ´€âƒ´€ guide/\
âƒ´‚       âƒ´ƒ´âƒ´€âƒ´€ YYYY-MM-DD-title.md  ( * as many manuals as published * )\
âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ _config.yml              # Jekyll settings & timezone enforcement\
âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ favicon.svg              # 16x16 Pixel Art\
âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ index.html               # Homepage with dynamic category routing\
âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ LICENSE                  # GPLv3 text\
âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ README.md                # This file\
âƒ´ƒ´âƒ´€âƒ´€ styles.css               # Catppuccin theme & typography limits\
```\
\
## Publishing Workflow\
\
### 1. Create a Post\
Create a new Markdown file inside either `_posts/blog/` or `_posts/guide/`. The filename **must** follow the `YYYY-MM-DD-title.md` format.\
\
At the very top of the file, insert the YAML front matter:\
```yaml\
---\
layout: default\
title: "Your Post Title Here"\
category: blog   # or "guide"\
---\
```\
Write your content directly below the second `---` using standard Markdown.\
\
### 2. Format the Code (Optional but Recommended)\
Run Prettier to ensure all markdown spacing, HTML indentation, and CSS syntax remain perfectly formatted:\
```bash\
npx prettier --write "**/*.{html,css,md,yml}"\
```\
\
### 3. Test Locally\
Preview the changes on your Fedora environment before pushing to the live site:\
```bash\
jekyll serve\
```\
*(If port 4000 is blocked, append `--port 4001`).*\
\
### 4. Deploy to GitHub Pages\
Push the new markdown files to the repository. GitHub Actions will automatically detect the push, compile the Jekyll site, and update the live domain within 60 seconds.\
```bash\
git add .\
git commit -m "Publish: [Post Title]"\
git push\
```\
EOF\
