\
# 5. Create a sample Typeset Document post matching main.pdf\
cat << 'EOF' > _posts/typeset/2026-10-10-dpss-mun-proposal.md\
---\
layout: default\
title: "DPSS MUN: First Interschool Edition Proposal"\
category: typeset\
---\
\
# DPSS MUN: First Interschool Edition Proposal\
\
Drafting a comprehensive structural framework for a Model United Nations conference requires meticulous attention to detail. This document serves as the official Proposal and Letter of Patronage for the inaugural interschool edition of DPSS MUN. \
\
Rather than relying on ad-hoc planning, this document establishes a rigid structural framework. It codifies governance and decision rights, establishes "Fixed Points" for operations, and even implements mathematical algorithms for logistics, such as calculating delegate capacities and financial viability.[^1]\
\
You can download the compiled PDF below. Be sure to move `main.pdf` into your `assets/pdf/` directory before clicking download.\
\
<div class="document-card">\
    <div class="document-info">\
        <span class="document-filename">main.pdf</span>\
        <a href="{{ '/assets/pdf/main.pdf' | relative_url }}" class="document-download" download>\
            <i data-lucide="download"></i> Download PDF\
        </a>\
    </div>\
    <img src="{{ '/assets/img/dummy-thumb.svg' | relative_url }}" class="document-thumbnail" alt="DPSS MUN Proposal Thumbnail">\
</div>\
\
[^1]: Typesetting this in LaTeX was essential to cleanly format the complex decision matrices, risk registers, and algorithmic parameter sheets while maintaining a strict academic aesthetic.\
EOF\
\
